@startuml 02_change1_state_class
!pragma layout smetana
title Change1 - new pattern instance: State\n"Maintenance Schedule Workflow" (code after Change4)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFE0B2
  BorderColor Black
}
hide empty members

class MaintenanceService <<Client>> {
  +StartAsync(id, request)
  +CompleteAsync(id, request)
  +CancelAsync(id, request)
  -TransitionAsync(id, label, request, transition)
}
note left of MaintenanceService
  Service/MaintenanceService.cs:97-111
  builds the context and calls
  context.Start / Complete / Cancel;
  no switch or if on Status
end note

class MaintenanceContext <<Context>> {
  +Schedule : MaintenanceSchedule
  +Car : Car
  +Now : DateTime
  +State : IMaintenanceState
  +Start()
  +Complete()
  +Cancel()
  +TransitionTo(next : IMaintenanceState)
}
note right of MaintenanceContext
  Service/Maintenance/MaintenanceContext.cs:7-42
  picks the state object from
  Schedule.Status by dictionary lookup;
  TransitionTo keeps State and
  Schedule.Status in step
end note

interface IMaintenanceState <<State>> {
  +Status : MaintenanceStatus
  +Start(context : MaintenanceContext)
  +Complete(context : MaintenanceContext)
  +Cancel(context : MaintenanceContext)
}

abstract class MaintenanceStateBase {
  +Start(context)
  +Complete(context)
  +Cancel(context)
  #ReleaseCar(context)
}
note right of MaintenanceStateBase
  default for all three operations:
  throw ApiException (409 Conflict)
end note

class ScheduledState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +Start(context)
  +Cancel(context)
}
class InProgressState <<ConcreteState>> {
  +Complete(context)
  +Cancel(context)
}
class CompletedState <<ConcreteState>>
class CancelledState <<ConcreteState>>

class MaintenanceSchedule <<entity>> #FFFFFF {
  +Status : MaintenanceStatus
  +StartedAt : DateTime?
  +CompletedAt : DateTime?
}
class Car <<entity>> #FFFFFF {
  +Status : CarStatus
  +IsAvailable : bool
}

MaintenanceService ..> MaintenanceContext : <<create>>
MaintenanceContext --> IMaintenanceState : current state
MaintenanceContext --> MaintenanceSchedule
MaintenanceContext --> Car
IMaintenanceState <|.. MaintenanceStateBase
MaintenanceStateBase <|-- ScheduledState
MaintenanceStateBase <|-- InProgressState
MaintenanceStateBase <|-- CompletedState
MaintenanceStateBase <|-- CancelledState
ScheduledState ..> InProgressState : TransitionTo on Start
ScheduledState ..> CancelledState : TransitionTo on Cancel
InProgressState ..> CompletedState : TransitionTo on Complete
InProgressState ..> CancelledState : TransitionTo on Cancel

legend bottom
  Each concrete state is a stateless shared instance (Instance).
  CompletedState and CancelledState override nothing, so every
  operation on a finished job returns 409.
  White classes are entities, not pattern roles.
endlegend
@enduml
